{
  "_id": "tg-singing",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "Then sang Moses, Ex. 15:1 (Deut. 32:44; Rev. 15:3). Miriam answered them, Sing ye to the Lord, Ex. 15:21. this song shall testify against them, Deut. 31:21. Then sang Deborah and Barak, Judg. 5:1. did they not sing one to another, 1 Sam. 21:11. David spake … the words of this song, 2 Sam. 22:1. his songs were a thousand and five, 1 Kgs. 4:32. Sing unto the Lord, all the earth, 1 Chr. 16:23 (Ps. 96:1). they sang together by course in praising, Ezra 3:11. When the morning stars sang together, Job 38:7 (D&C 128:23). sing praise to the name of the Lord, Ps. 7:17 (9:2, 11; 13:6; 18:49; 21:13; 33:2; 47:6, 7; 57:7–10; 59:16; 61:8; 66:2; 67:4; 71:22; 75:9; 106:12; 108:1; 135:3; 146:2; 147:1, 7; 150:1–6; James 5:13; D&C 138:24). he hath put a new song in my mouth, Ps. 40:3 (144:9; Isa. 42:10). sing unto the Lord a new song, Ps. 98:1 (Isa. 12:5). come before his presence with singing, Ps. 100:2. they shall sing in the ways of the Lord, Ps. 138:5. let them sing aloud upon their beds, Ps. 149:5. Jehovah is my strength and my song, Isa. 12:2. not drink wine with a song, Isa. 24:9. Then shall … the tongue of the dumb sing, Isa. 35:6. come to Zion with songs and everlasting joy upon their heads, Isa. 35:10 (51:11; 2 Ne. 8:11; D&C 45:71; 66:11; 101:18; 109:39; 133:33; Moses 7:53). break forth into singing, Isa. 44:23 (3 Ne. 22:1).",
